Well, I beat the odds and actually cranked out a preliminary Pirate
Patch. It wasn't as hard as I thought it would be (though I haven't
yet implemented the quest - it's currently just a copy of the Tourist
quest). And Rob, if you like, I could write up what needs to be done
in order to add a new class.

You can download the diff at my website (see sig for url).

A few details and questions:

Pirates can only be chaotic and human. (No other races seem to be
seafaring and the idea of a non-chaotic pirate seems rather silly.)

The quest artifact is The Treasure Map of Blackbeard, a scroll of
magic mapping that is fireproof, waterproof and won't disappear when
read. Carrying it grants ESP and auto-searching, invoking does object
detection.
Too powerful, too stupid?

X-level intrinsics:
level 7: stealth (with cat-like tread)
level 11: speed

More, less?

Starting pet will be a parrot (new monster) or monkey, unless your
preference is set to a dog or cat.

Role based name substitutions:
booze <=> rum
cram ration <=> sea biscuit
scimitar <=> cutlass (yes I know they're not really the same but ...)

Any more?

